// Quest step 1 trigger — Lord British's message (shared/docs/wiring.md
// "Quest step 1: LORDBRIT"). A shape-73 UnkEgg (DD-007a dispatch: quality
// = class_id - 0x47F, hatch range packed into the placed item's npcNum
// nibbles) whose hatch() spawns the pinned TypeLordBritish class's use()
// event — the cross-class spawn convention the codegen already emits for
// `spawn TypeXXX() -> return;` (push this, spawn this_size=0x04, target
// class:offset 0x0080, i.e. that class's FIRST compiled function). Manifest
// class pre-registration (build_eusecode.py step 2, "Pre-register every
// manifest-pinned class name") makes TypeLordBritish (pinned 0x05A3)
// resolve here regardless of compile order — verified by test_new_dialogue
// / build_eusecode.py's Gate 4 (QUEST_CRITICAL_CLASSES) and Gate 6
// (disassembly). Modeled on EGGSPIKE.UNK (DD-007 spike).

uses "egg";

globalflag lbStarted;

eggclass EggLBScene inherits Egg
{
	process hatch();
}

process EggLBScene::hatch()
{
	item : Item;

	// Two placements ship (Tenebrae gate primary + Map 8 Mythran-approach
	// backstop). The scene destroys only the apparition it runs at; the
	// OTHER pair's ghost item would stand around forever (seen in-game
	// 2026-07-04: the backstop ghost loitering in Mythran's house after
	// the Tenebrae scene played). If the scene already started anywhere,
	// this egg's one hatch is spent on cleanup instead: remove the
	// adjacent apparition (placed 96-150 units away; 256 covers both
	// placements with margin).
	if lbStarted = 1 {
		foreach item where type = TypeLordBritish within 256 of referent {
			item.destroy();
		}
		return;
	}

	spawn TypeLordBritish() -> return;
}
